From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dynamic Devices <engineering@dynamicdevices.co.uk>
Date: Thu, 17 Sep 2026 15:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] bytemuck: drop removed LaneCount bound

Rust removed core::simd::LaneCount and SupportedLaneCount in January 2026.
Chromium's vendored bytemuck already has a post-removal implementation,
but the pinned Yocto Rust build selected the older conditional branch and
failed with E0425/E0405. Use the same bound as the post-removal branch in
that older branch. This is limited to the kiosk's pinned Rust 1.98.1 build.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [pinned Yocto Rust/Chromium integration]

---
 third_party/rust/chromium_crates_io/vendor/bytemuck-v1/src/pod.rs      | 1 -
 third_party/rust/chromium_crates_io/vendor/bytemuck-v1/src/zeroable.rs | 1 -
 2 files changed, 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/third_party/rust/chromium_crates_io/vendor/bytemuck-v1/src/pod.rs b/third_party/rust/chromium_crates_io/vendor/bytemuck-v1/src/pod.rs
--- a/third_party/rust/chromium_crates_io/vendor/bytemuck-v1/src/pod.rs
+++ b/third_party/rust/chromium_crates_io/vendor/bytemuck-v1/src/pod.rs
@@ -153,5 +153,4 @@ unsafe impl<T, const N: usize> Pod for core::simd::Simd<T, N>
 where
   T: core::simd::SimdElement + Pod,
-  core::simd::LaneCount<N>: core::simd::SupportedLaneCount,
 {
 }

diff --git a/third_party/rust/chromium_crates_io/vendor/bytemuck-v1/src/zeroable.rs b/third_party/rust/chromium_crates_io/vendor/bytemuck-v1/src/zeroable.rs
--- a/third_party/rust/chromium_crates_io/vendor/bytemuck-v1/src/zeroable.rs
+++ b/third_party/rust/chromium_crates_io/vendor/bytemuck-v1/src/zeroable.rs
@@ -232,5 +232,4 @@ unsafe impl<T, const N: usize> Zeroable for core::simd::Simd<T, N>
 where
   T: core::simd::SimdElement + Zeroable,
-  core::simd::LaneCount<N>: core::simd::SupportedLaneCount,
 {
 }
